Note

When pnpm 12 is declared via the legacy `packageManager` field and [`pmOnFail`](/settings/cli#pmonfail) is not set to `ignore`, its resolution info is written to `pnpm-lock.yaml`. The lockfile then gains a leading [env lockfile document](/lockfile).

Since v12.0.0-rc.6, the field can also name [another package manager](/package-managers) — `npm`, `yarn` or `bun` — which is what `pnpm add npm@11` writes.
